  "final_answer": "I have gathered all the information needed. Let me provide the final answer.\n\n## Answer: The Most Recent Nobel Prize Winner in Physics (2025)\n\nThe **2025 Nobel Prize in Physics** was awarded jointly to three scientists:\n\n### Laureates:\n1. **John Clarke** \n2. **Michel H. Devoret**\n3. **John M. Martinis**\n\n### Their Contribution:\nThey were awarded the prize **\"for the discovery of macroscopic quantum mechanical tunnelling and energy quantisation in an electric circuit.\"**\n\n### Details of Their Work:\n- They conducted experiments with an electrical circuit that demonstrated **quantum mechanical tunnelling** and **quantised energy levels** in a system big enough to be held in the hand.\n- This breakthrough addresses a fundamental question in physics: the **maximum size of a system that can demonstrate quantum mechanical effects**.\n- Their work has opened pathways for developing the **next generation of quantum technology**, including:\n  - Quantum cryptography\n  - Quantum computers\n  - Quantum sensors\n\n### Significance:\nTheir discovery bridges the gap between microscopic quantum phenomena and macroscopic, human-scale systems, proving that quantum effects can be observed in tangible, everyday-scale objects. This paves the way for practical quantum technological applications.\n\n*Source: Official Nobel Prize website (nobelprize.org)*",
